Use Git’s [conditional includes](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-config#_conditional_includes). I added this to [home/home.nix](/home/thom/src/github.com/tteggel/.dotfiles/home/home.nix:479):

```nix
includes = [
  {
    condition = "gitdir:~/src/github.com/bookcreator/";
    contents.user.email = "thom@bookcreator.com";
  }
];
```

After your next `nswitch`, new commits automatically use:

- **Book Creator repos**, including nested directories: `thom@bookcreator.com`
- **Everywhere else:** `thom@tteggel.org`

This sets both author and committer email; your name stays `Thom Leggett`. Existing repo-local settings or environment overrides still take precedence.

